  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected today into \ntonight. Some drought relief is possible, though flooding is not\nexpected. Showery conditions persist Friday into Saturday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA disturbance moving around an upper low across Quebec province\nwill help support a developing surface low along an approaching\noccluded front today. Rain will occur regionwide today. The \ndeveloping low will cross the Gulf of Maine tonight. Rain will \npersist early tonight, then taper to showers overnight. The \nsurface low exits across the Maritimes Friday, with a trof \nextending back across the forecast area, while the upper low \nbegins to move south across the region. Showers will persist \nacross the region Friday, with the better chances across \nnorthern areas. Could also have the slight chance of a \nthunderstorm Friday afternoon. The surface/upper lows vertically\nstack across the Maritimes Friday night into Saturday, slowing \nthe movement of the system. A disturbance moving around the \nMaritimes system will rotate across the region Saturday. Shower \nchances will persist Friday night into Saturday. The system then\nexits Saturday night into Sunday. The entire forecast area \nshould receive a soaking rain today through tonight. Generally \nexpect rainfall totals of a half to three quarters of an inch \nacross much of the forecast area today into Saturday, with areas\nof up to around an inch.",
